  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "qclaim.deps-refresh.318ceb9d8414",
      "claim_type": "evidence",
      "authority_effect": "none",
      "statement": "The scaffold refreshes 33 direct dependencies to their latest in-range versions and moves vitest and @vitest/coverage-v8 from 3.2.7 to 4.1.11, the first release fixing GHSA-82fw-gwwq-j7x9 (vulnerable range >=2.1.0 <4.1.11). vitest.config.ts drops a UserConfig plugins cast that vitest 4 makes unnecessary and gains coverage.include ['src/**/*.{ts,tsx}'], because vitest 4 removed coverage.all and without an include only test-loaded files are reported; reported files go from 36 of 125 to 105 and overall coverage from 77.58 percent to 53.64 percent, correcting a figure that was already wrong before this change rather than fixing a regression. Full-tree advisories fall from 31 to 2, both dev-path with no safe fix available. bun audit --prod reports no vulnerabilities. The engines.node declaration of >=20.0.0 is left untouched and is known to be inaccurate independently of this change, since @supabase/supabase-js has required Node >=22.0.0 as a production dependency since before this branch. This receipt binds only the listed changed paths at the subject commit. It grants no merge, admission, runtime, or fleet-rollout authority and establishes no owner review.",
      "evidence_paths": [
        ".quirk/evidence/deps-refresh-17d73fee5cfe.json",
        ".quirk/evidence/deps-refresh-1f86b7ab2367.json",
        "bun.lock",
        "package.json",
        "vitest.config.ts"
      ]
    }
